{:edb/db-before-t 1178 :edb/db-after-t 1179 :edb/tx-data [[1110 62 "Activity-type enum selecting the distribution's use, initially activity.type/lesson or activity.type/review. Reuses the enums defined in content/0-activity.edn." 13194139534491 17592186045436 false] [1110 62 "Activity-type enum selecting the distribution's use: activity.type/lesson, activity.type/review, or activity.type/assessment. Reuses the enums defined in content/0-activity.edn." 13194139534491 17592186045436 true] [13194139534491 50 #inst "2026-10-11T23:24:06.278Z" 13194139534491 17592186045436 true] [17592186045526 62 "Requires an activity type and all six weights when explicitly ensured. The application checks allowed activity types, finite nonnegative weights, a positive finite total for each distribution, exactly one policy owner, and one record per activity type in that policy. Weights are normalized across eligible bands before selecting a fresh question within the chosen band; an unavailable question supply is not learner failure. Stopping rules remain application code." 13194139534491 17592186045436 false] [17592186045526 62 "Requires an activity type and all six weights when explicitly ensured. The application supports lessons, reviews, and assessments and checks finite nonnegative weights, a positive finite total for each distribution, exactly one policy owner, and one record per activity type in that policy. Lessons and reviews choose the phase using their stopping rules; ordinary assessments use initial weights throughout, while a designated assessment retake/recheck explicitly requests remedial weights. Weights are normalized across eligible bands before selecting a fresh question within the chosen band; an unavailable question supply is not learner failure. Stopping rules and retake scheduling remain application code." 13194139534491 17592186045436 true] [17592186409231 1091 #edb/ref 17592186423043 13194139534491 17592186045436 true] [17592186423043 1110 #edb/ref 17592186045460 1